This directory is a clone of FsToolkit.ErrorHandling. We want to know whether the existing tests for the `Result.require*` functions in `tests/FsToolkit.ErrorHandling.Tests` catch realistic defects in `src/FsToolkit.ErrorHandling/Result.fs`.

The `mutants/` directory holds four candidate defects as patches: `M1.patch`, `M2.patch`, `M3.patch`, and `M4.patch`. For each candidate, find out whether the existing tests detect it. Use the `net9.0` target framework. Do not add or change tests.

Write `mutation-report.json` in this directory with this shape:

```json
{
  "baseline": { "command": "<the test command you ran>", "passed": 0, "failed": 0 },
  "mutants": [
    { "id": "M1", "detected": true, "failingTests": ["<full test name>"], "explanation": "<one or two sentences>" }
  ]
}
```

Give one entry for each of M1, M2, M3, and M4. `detected` is `true` or `false`. List the full names of the tests that failed because of the candidate in `failingTests`, or give an empty list.
